-- title:
--   Lattice criterion for the prime Hecke set at ℓ
-- statement:
--   Fix $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and write $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$. Let $R\subseteq\mathbb{H}$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule that is an order in the sense of the project predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): $1\in R$, $R$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $R$ is all of $\mathbb{H}$, and $R$ is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Let $\ell$ be a prime, let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell\in v$, and let $\varphi\colon \mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v\to M_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ be a ring isomorphism onto $2\times2$ matrices over the $v$-adic completion such that $\varphi(1\otimes r)=r\cdot 1$ for every $r$, and assume that $z$ lies in [`Submodule.localBox R v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) — the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z'\otimes c$ with $z'\in R$ and $c$ in the $v$-adic integers — precisely when all four entries $\varphi(z)_{ij}$ are $v$-adic integers. Let $x$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$ and let $J\subseteq\mathbb{H}$ be any $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule. Throughout, [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox R`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) denotes the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$ generated by the $z'\otimes \alpha$ with $z'\in R$ and $\alpha$ an everywhere-integral finite adele, and [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele R g`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) denotes the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of elements of $\mathbb{H}$ whose image in $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$ lies in $g\cdot$`finiteAdeleBox R`. The assertion is the equivalence of the following two conditions: (i) there is an $h$ in [`QuaternionAlgebra.primeHeckeSet R ℓ`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_ClassSetHecke.html#L109), i.e. a unit $h$ with $h\in$`finiteAdeleBox R`, $\ell\, h^{-1}\in$`finiteAdeleBox R`, $h^{-1}\notin$`finiteAdeleBox R` and $\ell^{-1}h\notin$`finiteAdeleBox R`, such that $J=$`ofFiniteIdele R (x * h)`; and (ii) $J\subseteq$`ofFiniteIdele R x`, every $z\in$`ofFiniteIdele R x` satisfies $\ell z\in J$, $J=$`ofFiniteIdele R y` for some unit $y$, and the relative index of the additive subgroup underlying $J$ in that underlying `ofFiniteIdele R x` equals $\ell^2$.
--
--   This is the lattice-theoretic half of Eichler's description of the Hecke correspondence at $\ell$ on right $R$-ideal classes: it identifies the right ideals $J$ obtained from the prime Hecke set at $\ell$ with the locally free right $R$-ideals sandwiched as $\ell I_x\subseteq J\subseteq I_x$ of index $\ell^2$, where $I_x$ is the ideal attached to the finite idèle $x$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where the counts of such ideals are matched with counts of subgroups in kernels of dual pairs.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_exists_mem_primeHeckeSet_eq_ofFiniteIdele_mul_iff.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_QuaternionAlgebra_ClassSetHecke
import Definitions.Def_Submodule_LocalBox

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open scoped TensorProduct Quaternion Pointwise
open IsDedekindDomain NumberField

theorem QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder.exists_mem_primeHeckeSet_eq_ofFiniteIdele_mul_iff {a b : ℚ}
    {R : Submodule ℤ ℍ[ℚ, a, b]} (hR : QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder R) {ℓ : ℕ} (hℓ : ℓ.Prime)
    (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 ℚ)) (hv : (ℓ : 𝓞 ℚ) ∈ v.asIdeal)
    (φ : ℍ[ℚ, a, b] ⊗[ℚ] v.adicCompletion ℚ ≃+* Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) (v.adicCompletion ℚ))
    (hφ : ∀ r : v.adicCompletion ℚ,
      φ ((1 : ℍ[ℚ, a, b]) ⊗ₜ[ℚ] r) = r • (1 : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) (v.adicCompletion ℚ)))
    (hRv : ∀ z : ℍ[ℚ, a, b] ⊗[ℚ] v.adicCompletion ℚ,
      z ∈ Submodule.localBox R v ↔ ∀ i j, φ z i j ∈ v.adicCompletionIntegers ℚ)
    (x : (ℍ[ℚ, a, b] ⊗[ℚ] FiniteAdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ)ˣ) (J : Submodule ℤ ℍ[ℚ, a, b]) :
    (∃ h ∈ QuaternionAlgebra.primeHeckeSet R ℓ, J = Submodule.ofFiniteIdele R (x * h)) ↔
      (J ≤ Submodule.ofFiniteIdele R x ∧
        (∀ z ∈ Submodule.ofFiniteIdele R x, (ℓ : ℚ) • z ∈ J) ∧
        (∃ y : (ℍ[ℚ, a, b] ⊗[ℚ] FiniteAdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ)ˣ, J = Submodule.ofFiniteIdele R y) ∧
        J.toAddSubgroup.relIndex (Submodule.ofFiniteIdele R x).toAddSubgroup = ℓ ^ 2) := by sorry
